  ('leaving-work-at-work', 187, 'Wipe down your work surface at home at the end of the day and set one personal object on it.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 188, 'Put a sticky note on your fridge with tonight''s plan, so you see it when you walk in.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 189, 'Choose a calm phrase to repeat when work thoughts creep in this evening: "That belongs to tomorrow."'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 190, 'On a rainy evening, listen to the rain for two minutes before turning on any screen.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 191, 'In summer, take an after-work swim, a run through the sprinkler or a cool shower to mark the change.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 192, 'When it is already dark as you leave work, look up at the evening sky for a moment before heading home.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 193, 'During your busy season, write down the date it ends and one thing you will do to celebrate.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 194, 'In a crunch at work, protect one small thing every evening, like a ten-minute walk or a phone call.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 195, 'When work gets busy, tell the people at home what to expect and when things will ease.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 196, 'Look at the work still on your plate tonight and choose one thing to move to next week.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 197, 'Give yourself one hour this weekend that you would usually spend thinking about work, and fill it with something fun.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 198, 'Remove your work email from your laptop''s start-up apps so it does not open on its own on your days off.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 199, 'Sign out of your work account on your personal tablet or e-reader.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 200, 'Set up a separate browser profile for work and close it at the end of the day.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 201, 'Unpin work tabs from your personal browser so they do not greet you every time you open it.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 202, 'Put a time limit on work apps on your phone for the evening hours.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 203, 'Write a short message to a coworker thanking them for something, and send it before you log off.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 204, 'Tell one coworker about a hobby you enjoy, so they know you outside of work too.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 205, 'Bring something from home to your workspace that reminds you of life outside work, like a photo or a postcard.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 206, 'If you work at home with kids around, give them a signal that work is over, like a high five or a knock on the table.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 207, 'If you work from your couch or bed, move work to a table today, even a small one, so the bed stays for rest.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 208, 'Write your usual work hours on a card and keep it in your wallet as a reminder of where the edges are.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 209, 'Look at your next week and choose one evening when you will leave exactly on time.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 210, 'Notice one task that keeps following you home, and ask a coworker or manager for help with it during work hours.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 211, 'Make a simple template for handing off unfinished work to the next shift so you leave fewer loose ends.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 212, 'If you work in sales, set a time each evening after which you stop checking your numbers.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 213, 'If you carry a separate work phone, power it down when you clock out and leave it off until your next shift.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 214, 'Ask a teammate to swap an on-call weekend with you once if it would protect something that matters to you.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 215, 'Sleep in on your next day off without setting an alarm, if your life allows it.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 216, 'Stop work five minutes earlier than usual today and use those minutes to tidy up and plan.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 217, 'Write your three biggest wins of the week on your last workday afternoon, then close the laptop.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 218, 'Schedule an encouraging text to yourself that arrives at your next start time, so tonight you can stop thinking about it.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 219, 'Notice what you do with your free evening when work is not in it, and write down one thing you enjoyed.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 220, 'If your workplace has a time clock, take a breath as you punch out and say, "That''s the shift."'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 221, 'Write one work worry on a slip of paper, drop it in a jar by the door, and close the lid until morning.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 222, 'Before going home, picture the work you finished as boxes on a shelf, labeled and set down for the night.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 223, 'Go outside for a few minutes after you log off and notice the weather, as a way of checking in on the world beyond your job.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 224, 'Choose an "after work" scent, like a hand lotion or a tea, and use it only once the workday is over.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 225, 'Make a list of the parts of you that have nothing to do with your job, like friend, cook, gardener or fan, and spend time as one of them tonight.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 226, 'Mention to your manager at your next check-in that you are working on wrapping up on time, and ask which tasks matter most late in the day.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 227, 'Ask a coworker how they switch off after work, and try their idea this week.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 228, 'Plan your next vacation, even a short one, and put the dates on the calendar today.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 229, 'During a vacation, tuck your work laptop into a suitcase pocket or hotel safe and leave it there.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 230, 'On the day before a vacation, set aside your last hour to tie up loose ends, rather than staying late.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 231, 'On the last afternoon before a long weekend, write a simple list for your first morning back so you can stop thinking about it.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 232, 'Write down how you want to feel at the end of your next day off, and plan one thing that would help.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 233, 'Do something on your day off that you cannot do on a workday, like a weekday matinee or a morning hike.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 234, 'On a weekend morning, take a slow walk with a coffee and no earbuds.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 235, 'Go to a farmers market, a yard sale or the library this weekend and leave your work thoughts at home.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 236, 'Try a new recipe on a free afternoon and give each step your full attention.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 237, 'If you are tempted to work on a Sunday, write the task on your list for your next workday instead and close the laptop.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 238, 'Notice if Sunday afternoon starts to fill with work thoughts, and go outside for twenty minutes.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 239, 'Make a plan for your first hour back before the weekend starts, so the weekend itself is free from planning.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 240, 'When you leave work at the end of your week, say out loud, "See you next week."'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 241, 'If your weekend falls midweek, still give it a clear start and finish, like a special breakfast and an early night.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 242, 'Send your last work email by your finishing time today, then shut the inbox.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 243, 'Write your finishing time on a sticky note at the start of the day and put it where you will see it often.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 244, 'Tell your family or roommates what time you will be done with work today, so they can help you keep it.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 245, 'Ask someone at home to call you for dinner at your finishing time, and go when they call.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 246, 'Write your handoff notes clearly if you work in a hospital or care home, so no one needs to call you after your shift.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 247, 'If you work at a call center, take off your headset slowly at the end of the shift and stretch your neck.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 248, 'If you work a register, rub your hands together for a few seconds after clocking out and let them rest.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 249, 'If you work construction, leave your boots and hard hat in the garage or truck instead of carrying them through the house.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 250, 'If you work in a salon, wipe down your station last thing and let that be your closing ritual.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 251, 'If you teach, write tomorrow''s lesson goal on the board before you leave, so it waits in the classroom and not in your head.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 252, 'If you are a home health aide, keep a small notebook in your bag for client notes, and close it when you get home.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 253, 'If you work at a restaurant, eat a real meal sitting down after your shift, not standing up in the kitchen.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 254, 'If caregiving is your trade, call or text someone who cares for you after your shift ends.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 255, 'Small business owners can pick one day each week to leave sales figures and reviews unchecked; choose yours today.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 256, 'If you juggle more than one job, write the schedule for both on one calendar tonight, so you can see your real free hours and protect them.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 257, 'If you work nights, share a small after-work breakfast with someone you live with, and talk about anything but the shift.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 258, 'If you deliver for an app, choose your last zone near home so the end of the shift is close to your door.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 259, 'If you volunteer as well as work, keep one evening a week free from both.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 260, 'Pick up an instrument, a sketchbook or a crossword for twenty minutes tonight.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 261, 'Lie on the floor for three minutes when you get home, legs up on a chair or couch, and let the workday drain out of your shoulders.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 262, 'Text a friend a funny photo after work, something with no connection to your job.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 263, 'Plan a regular weeknight with friends, like trivia night or a walk, and keep it on the calendar.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 264, 'Write a list of what you love about your home, and read it on an evening when work feels big.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 265, 'Spend five minutes looking at photos from a trip or a happy day after work.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 266, 'Put work books and papers away on a shelf you cannot see from your bed.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 267, 'If you bring papers home, give them one shelf or bin, and put them there the moment you walk in.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 268, 'Swap your phone for an old-fashioned alarm clock tonight so there is no reason to pick up the phone in bed.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 269, 'Put a rubber band or a sticky note around your work phone at night as a small reminder to leave it alone until morning.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 270, 'Write a "tomorrow" list before bed and leave it in the kitchen, not by your bed.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 271, 'Plan a short walk after dinner with someone you live with, and talk about anything except your jobs.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 272, 'Choose one room in your home where work is never allowed, and tell the people you live with.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 273, 'Practice saying "I''m off the clock today" with a smile, for when someone brings up work at a party or dinner.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 274, 'If a neighbor or friend asks about your job, share one sentence, then ask about their weekend.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 275, 'Join a group unrelated to your work, like a choir, a book club or a pottery class.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 276, 'Rest for twenty minutes after a long shift before you start any chores at home.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 277, 'Do something tonight just because it is fun, with no goal and nothing to show for it afterward.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 278, 'When you get home, look in the mirror and say, "Welcome home."'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 279, 'If you manage people, tell your team plainly that you do not expect replies after hours, and mean it.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 280, 'Ask a coworker to walk out with you at the end of the day this week, so leaving on time feels easier.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 281, 'Mark the end of your workweek with a small ritual, like ordering takeout or watching a favorite show.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 282, 'Write down three good things that happened outside work today.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 283, 'If you are stuck on a work problem at night, write it down to revisit in the morning, when a rested mind may see it differently.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 284, 'Write one sentence in a journal tonight about your life outside your job.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 285, 'Watch the sky change color after work, from a window, a porch or a park.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 286, 'If you work outdoors, wash your hands and face and change shirts before you sit down to eat.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 287, 'If you are a parent working from home, close your work door when the kids get home from school, even for an hour.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 288, 'Ask yourself before you open the laptop tonight: will doing this now make tomorrow better, or just make tonight worse?'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 289, 'Picture your favorite place outside of work for one minute before you fall asleep.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 290, 'Take your time on a weekend chore you usually rush, like folding laundry or washing the dishes, and let it be slow.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 291, 'On a holiday morning, spend one hour doing nothing in particular, and let that be enough.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 292, 'Spend a free evening this week on something that leaves you a little tired in a good way, like dancing, swimming or a long bike ride.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 293, 'List every place work reaches you at home, like email, chat, texts or a calendar app, and pick one to quiet tonight.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 294, 'Turn off notification previews for work email so a subject line cannot grab your attention at dinner.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 295, 'Hide your work calendar on your phone after your finishing time, if your calendar app allows it.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 296, 'Log out of work chat on your personal computer tonight.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 297, 'Make your phone''s lock screen a photo from your life outside work.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 298, 'Keep your phone in your bag during dinner with friends tonight, and let work messages wait until you get home.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 299, 'Ask your team to add their working hours to the shared calendar, and start by adding yours.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 300, 'Say "I''m heading out, see you tomorrow" to your team out loud or in chat, so your leaving is clear.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 301, 'When an after-hours message arrives, ask yourself whether it is urgent or simply sent late, and answer to match.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 302, 'If a client emails on the weekend, reply on your next workday with a cheerful note and no apology for the wait.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 303, 'When you see a work message late at night, put the phone down, write one word about it on paper, and let it be.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 304, 'If work truly needs you after hours, set a firm end time for that stretch and stop when it arrives.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 305, 'After a late work call, take a short walk or stretch before you go to bed.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 306, 'Choose a "no work after" time for the weekend, like six o''clock on your last workday, and keep to it.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 307, 'Spend a Saturday morning in pajamas with a book, without opening a single work file.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 308, 'Visit a museum, a zoo or a botanical garden on your next day off and leave the laptop at home.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 309, 'Take photos of things you find beautiful on a weekend walk, just for you, not to post.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 310, 'Plan something fun for the first night of your weekend so the end of the workweek feels like a celebration.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 311, 'On a summer weekend, head to a pool, a beach or a lake and leave your work phone at home.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 312, 'During the holidays, write down which days you will be fully off and share them with your team early.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 313, 'On a winter weekend, make a pot of soup or bake bread, and let the long cooking time slow your mind down.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 314, 'Spend the first hour of a day off outside, before you look at any screen.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 315, 'If you care for people at work and at home, ask someone to take one evening task so you get thirty minutes to yourself.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 316, 'If you teach, choose a stretch of the summer break with no lesson planning at all, and write the dates on your calendar.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 317, 'If you work retail during the holiday rush, plan one cozy thing to look forward to after each long shift.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 318, 'Post your shop''s holiday hours early if you own a small business, and plan your own time off around them.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 319, 'If you work weekends, plan something you love for your next weekday off and tell a friend about it.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 320, 'Write down your honest answer to this question: "What is part of my job, and what is not?"'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 321, 'Choose one thing you will stop doing after hours, like checking the schedule app, and skip it tonight.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 322, 'Ask a coworker which work alerts they turn off after hours, and try turning off the same ones.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 323, 'Pick one day off this month to go without work email entirely.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 324, 'Write a gentle reminder on your bathroom mirror with a dry-erase marker: "You''re off the clock."'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 325, 'At dinner, invite everyone at the table to share a good moment from their day that happened away from work or school.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 326, 'Sit on your porch, stoop or balcony after work and watch the street for five minutes.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 327, 'Ask yourself at nine o''clock tonight, "Where is my mind?" and if it is at work, bring it back to the room you are in.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 328, 'Write a short "good enough" list of three things you did today that were enough, even if they were not perfect.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 329, 'Leave one reply in your drafts folder until tomorrow morning, and send it then.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 330, 'Give a nagging task a clear time slot on tomorrow''s calendar, so it stops nagging at you tonight.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 331, 'Ask someone you live with what they would like to do this weekend, and plan it together.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 332, 'Plan one evening this week when every work device stays switched off from dinner to bedtime.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 333, 'Write a short letter to yourself about why your time off matters, and keep it where you will find it.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 334, 'Say to yourself tonight, "My worth is not how fast I reply."'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 335, 'Notice one thing that brings you joy this evening, away from work, and say it out loud.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 336, 'Do something kind for a neighbor or friend this weekend, a reminder that your life is bigger than your job.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 337, 'If your job asks a lot of your heart, like counseling or social work, write down the hardest moment of the day, then tear up the page.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 338, 'If you work in emergency services, have a short debrief with a coworker before you leave, so the hard parts do not ride home alone with you.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 339, 'Change out of your scrubs before you head home after a hospital or clinic shift, if you can.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 340, 'If you drive for work, listen to any voicemails only after you have parked at home, then take one breath before you get out.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 341, 'If you work in a warehouse, shake out your arms and legs in the parking lot before you head home.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 342, 'If you work at a school, sit in a quiet classroom or hallway for one minute after the last bell.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 343, 'If you freelance, decide which days are your weekend and tell your regular clients when you are off.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 344, 'When someone asks what you do, mention one thing you love outside your job too.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 345, 'Try one evening without TV or social media and see what you fill it with instead.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 346, 'Invite a neighbor or friend to a porch chat, a card game or a short evening walk this week.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 347, 'Each time your hand reaches for your phone tonight, ask yourself, "Am I looking for work, or for something else?"'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 348, 'Write down one belief you hold about being always available, and ask whether it is really true.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 349, 'If your job never seems to end, write down what "done for today" looks like and use it as your finish line.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 350, 'Draw a line across your paper planner at your finishing time, a visible edge to the workday.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 351, 'End your workday by tidying one small thing at home, like the dishes, to shift your attention.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 352, 'When you get home, ask the first person you see about their day before you say anything about yours.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 353, 'Put on music you love while making dinner and sing along.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 354, 'If you start work early in the morning, decide the night before what you will wear and eat, so work thoughts do not fill your last hour.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 355, 'Download a podcast, comedy special or audiobook that has nothing to do with your field, and save it for the ride home as a passenger.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 356, 'Let a friend vent about their job this week, then help each other change the subject to something fun.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 357, 'Remember a time you left work behind fully, like on a great vacation, and write one thing you did then that you could try tonight.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 358, 'Write your shutdown steps on an index card and tape it near your work spot, so ending the day takes no thinking.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 359, 'Notice how your evening feels when you leave work at work, and write down one word for it.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 360, 'Before a big deadline, plan what you will do the evening after it is done, and make it something restful.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 361, 'Tell yourself, "Thank you for working hard today. Now you can rest."'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 362, 'Treat your bed as a work-free zone tonight: no laptop, no work phone, no planning.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 363, 'On a Sunday evening, put your phone away early and spend the last hours of the weekend on something cozy.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 364, 'Look back at what has helped most during this challenge so far, and pick one habit to carry into your ordinary weeks.'),
  ('leaving-work-at-work', 365, 'Hum or whistle on the walk from your workplace to the bus stop, as a cheerful way to say the day is done.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 1, 'Read one page of any book with your morning coffee before you look at your phone.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 2, 'Think back to a book you loved as a kid and write its plot, or what you remember of it, in two sentences.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 3, 'Pick up whatever book is closest to you right now and read the first paragraph, just to see if it pulls you in.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 4, 'Find out where your nearest public library is and what hours it keeps this week.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 5, 'Sign up for a library card, online or at the front desk, so books cost you nothing to try.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 6, 'Put your phone in another room for ten minutes tonight and spend that time with a few pages instead.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 7, 'Choose one cozy spot at home that will be your reading place, and set a pillow or blanket there.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 8, 'Ask a friend what the last book was that they couldn''t put down, and jot the answer in your notes app.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 9, 'Give yourself permission, out loud if you like, to stop reading any book that isn''t giving you pleasure.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 10, 'Read a short poem before bed and notice one image from it that stays with you.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 11, 'Browse the "staff picks" shelf at a library or bookstore and read the back cover of three of them.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 12, 'Place a hold on one book at your library, even if the wait list is long.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 13, 'Make a bookmark from a scrap of paper, a receipt or a ribbon, and tuck it into the book you''re reading.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 14, 'Reread the opening chapter of a favorite book and enjoy knowing what''s coming.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 15, 'Swap five minutes of scrolling at lunch for five minutes with a book or an ebook.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 16, 'Read a page aloud to yourself in a quiet room and listen to how the sentences sound.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 17, 'Clear a small stack of books off a shelf and put the one you most want to read on top.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 18, 'Download your library''s free reading app and connect it to your library card.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 19, 'Borrow an audiobook and listen to the first chapter while you fold laundry or wash dishes.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 20, 'Read a short story in one sitting, start to finish, while your tea is still warm.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 21, 'Leave a book on your nightstand tonight where your phone usually sits.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 22, 'Copy one line you loved from today''s reading onto a sticky note and put it somewhere you''ll see it.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 23, 'Visit a used bookstore and let yourself wander the aisles with no plan to buy anything.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 24, 'Read a comic or a graphic novel today and take your time with the pictures.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 25, 'Set a reading lamp or a small light by your favorite chair so the spot feels inviting after dark.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 26, 'Write down three kinds of stories you loved as a teenager, such as mysteries, adventure, or romance.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 27, 'Read on a park bench for as long as it feels good, then close the book and look around.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 28, 'Ask a librarian to suggest something light and fun, and tell them what you''ve enjoyed before.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 29, 'Pick a book purely because you like its cover, and read the first few pages to see if it''s a match.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 30, 'Tell someone at dinner about something you read today, even if it was a single paragraph.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 31, 'Read a recipe from a cookbook for pleasure, the way you''d read a short story, without planning to cook it.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 32, 'Find a little free library in your neighborhood, take a look inside, and borrow one book if anything catches your eye.'),
  ('reading-for-pleasure', 33, 'Carry a paperback or an ebook in your bag today so a few spare minutes can become reading minutes.'),
